    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (73.41), whose elite .443 xwOBA and platoon advantage against Tyler Mahle make him our highest-projected performer. He is joined by the high-upside speed threat **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.04), who benefits significantly from a 14% dynamic platoon boost and a leadoff role, helping offset the challenge posed by Chase Burns. **Trea Turner** (66.44) and **Chase Meidroth** (66.08) also provide strong value today; both players exploit the favorable matchup against left-handed starters, with **Chase Meidroth** benefiting from a substantial 17% SP skill adjustment. The lineup as a whole is bolstered by the venue, as **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich** gain a massive 16% park adjustment, keeping them safely in the \"Strong\" start tier despite the lack of confirmed opponent data.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Carson Benge** (55.47), who narrowly missed the cut for the final utility slot. While **Carson Benge** posted a respectable score bolstered by a 10% SP skill adjustment against Andrew Painter, he was ultimately edged out by the superior floor and platoon-adjusted efficiency of **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (58.86). Despite **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** facing a slight efficiency drag due to the elite hold threat, his raw power profile in a hitter-friendly environment remains a safer play for daily production. We continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Dillon Dingler** and **Junior Caminero**, as their projected scores remain volatile should their spots in the batting order shift significantly downward. Managers should note that while **Lars Nootbaar** (56.83) is starting, he faces a stiff test against Gerrit Cole; however, his dynamic platoon advantage remains high enough to warrant the start over the bench options.",
